{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6a23b882-10de-4a15-a33f-758b3c6251fa","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Intervals.icu OAuth integration has been fixed, and the root causes have been documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Connect Button Failing for Everyone (401 Unauthorized)**:\n   * **Cause**: In [`static/app.js`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/static/app.js), the Connect button was an HTML `\u003ca\u003e` link initiating document navigation to `/api/intervals/auth/init`. Document navigations do not send the `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` stored in `localStorage`, causing `server.py` to respond with `401 Unauthorized`.\n   * **Fix**: Updated [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/server.py) to support `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` returning `{ \"authorize_url\": ... }`, and updated [`static/app.js`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/static/app.js) so clicking Connect performs an authenticated `POST` request via `api()` before navigating via `window.location.assign`.\n\n2. **Authorize URL 400 `invalid_request` (Duplicate Scopes)**:\n   * **Cause**: In [`config.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/config.py), `SCOPES` requested both `:READ` and `:WRITE` for activity and calendar (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). In Intervals.icu, `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and duplicate scope categories cause Intervals to fail with an `invalid_request` error.\n   * **Fix**: Reduced `SCOPES` in [`config.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/config.py) to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Athletes Disconnected After 1 Hour (`status: expired, reconnect`)**:\n   * **Cause**: Intervals.icu tokens do not return `expires_in` or `refresh_token` and remain valid indefinitely until revoked. In [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/server.py), `store_connection()` fell back to a default 3600-second TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the background `refresh_tokens()` thread marked the token as expired when it found no refresh token after 1 hour.\n   * **Fix**: Updated [`server.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-dshQ0n/server.py) so tokens without an `expires_in` are stored as perpetual (no synthetic expiration), updated `refresh_tokens()` to skip them, and added lazy revocation detection (marking as `\"expired, reconnect\"` when Intervals API returns a 401).\n","duration_seconds":114.191199,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":141795,"output_tokens":5671,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":393097,"total_tokens":147466}}}
